# Migrations

The policy lives in [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) → **Migrations**, and the
runner contract in [`docs/spec/UPDATES.md`](../../docs/spec/UPDATES.md) → **State
migrations**. Read both before touching persisted state; this rule only points
there so the policy has one home.

In short: app code reads and writes the current schema only (no dual-read, no
legacy-cleanup code); state an earlier release wrote is brought up to date by a
migration in `backend/migrations/`, run on update; corrective repair of state the
app wrote wrong is normal engineering.
